1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:07,857
Meet Junction Lab, an interactive traffic simulation project inspired by the junction near I I T Delhi.

2
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:12,097
Explore mixed traffic, test signal settings, and compare control strategies.

3
00:00:13,717 --> 00:00:17,601
Five vehicle classes move through a left hand traffic junction.

4
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:24,204
Detailed procedural models, signal phases, turning movements, and live queue metrics make the simulation easy to inspect.

5
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:31,643
Change traffic demand, cycle length, or the green split, then restart with the same random seed.

6
00:00:31,643 --> 00:00:35,285
Watch queues form and discharge while delay and throughput update.

7
00:00:36,917 --> 00:00:42,317
Import traffic counts from C S V, map the columns, and inspect assumptions.

8
00:00:42,317 --> 00:00:48,549
The Python pipeline also provides parameter fitting and observation comparison tools for future field validation.

9
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:54,223
A separate native SUMO pipeline runs locally through Tra C I.

10
00:00:54,223 --> 00:01:00,517
Its recorded trajectories replay in the three dimensional viewer, with a timeline and explanations of controller decisions.

11
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:09,175
Compare fixed time, actuated, and queue pressure controllers across fifteen runs using five paired seeds.

12
00:01:09,175 --> 00:01:11,985
This synthetic example favors actuated control.

13
00:01:11,985 --> 00:01:15,732
The chart reports uncertainty, not real world savings.

14
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:22,951
The project includes result exports, arrival schedule checks, and twenty four automated tests.

15
00:01:22,951 --> 00:01:28,552
The browser simulator and native SUMO replay are clearly identified as separate engines.

16
00:01:30,183 --> 00:01:33,728
The current demonstration uses synthetic demand and assumed geometry.

17
00:01:33,728 --> 00:01:40,031
The next milestone is fitting the model to field data, then testing it against independent observations.
